1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,452
It compiled on my laptop. On the server: class not found. Every Java team has lived this.

2
00:00:07,002 --> 00:00:08,459
The code did not change.

3
00:00:08,459 --> 00:00:10,463
What changed is where Java looks,

4
00:00:10,463 --> 00:00:12,527
and what the environment tells it.

5
00:00:13,077 --> 00:00:16,544
Today you learn four ideas that explain it: packages,

6
00:00:16,544 --> 00:00:17,525
the class path,

7
00:00:17,525 --> 00:00:18,376
dependencies,

8
00:00:18,376 --> 00:00:20,992
and configuration from outside the code.

9
00:00:21,542 --> 00:00:24,187
Then you break the class path on purpose, and fix it.

10
00:00:26,237 --> 00:00:29,458
Four ideas. We will prove each one on a real machine.

11
00:00:30,008 --> 00:00:30,292
One.

12
00:00:30,292 --> 00:00:32,209
A package is a folder path.

13
00:00:32,209 --> 00:00:36,682
The class com dot cloud cart dot main lives in the folders com,

14
00:00:36,682 --> 00:00:37,462
cloud cart,

15
00:00:37,462 --> 00:00:38,456
main dot java.

16
00:00:39,006 --> 00:00:39,292
Two.

17
00:00:39,292 --> 00:00:43,577
The class path is the list of places Java looks for classes.

18
00:00:43,577 --> 00:00:45,148
Folders and jar files,

19
00:00:45,148 --> 00:00:47,220
separated by colons on Linux.

20
00:00:47,770 --> 00:00:48,150
Three.

21
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:50,749
A dependency is code somebody else wrote,

22
00:00:50,749 --> 00:00:52,651
usually shipped as a jar file.

23
00:00:52,651 --> 00:00:54,490
You add it to the class path.

24
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:55,371
Four.

25
00:00:55,371 --> 00:00:59,352
Configuration lives outside the code: environment variables,

26
00:00:59,352 --> 00:01:02,272
and properties you pass with dash capital D.

27
00:01:02,822 --> 00:01:07,366
Same program, different environment, different behavior. That is the whole point.

28
00:01:09,416 --> 00:01:12,403
Go to the shop folder. Type: CD, shop.

29
00:01:12,953 --> 00:01:17,646
What do we have? Type: find, src, lib, dash type, f, pipe, sort.

30
00:01:18,196 --> 00:01:23,871
One source file, inside folders that match its package. And one jar file, our dependency.

31
00:01:24,421 --> 00:01:30,927
Read the source. Type: cat, src, slash, com, slash, cloud cart, slash, main dot java.

32
00:01:31,477 --> 00:01:33,505
Line one declares the package.

33
00:01:33,505 --> 00:01:36,750
Line three imports a class from another package,

34
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:38,846
com dot cloud cart dot pricing.

35
00:01:38,846 --> 00:01:41,483
That class is not in our source folder.

36
00:01:42,033 --> 00:01:43,409
Compile it as it is.

37
00:01:43,409 --> 00:01:44,304
Type: java C,

38
00:01:44,304 --> 00:01:44,786
dash D,

39
00:01:44,786 --> 00:01:45,061
out,

40
00:01:45,061 --> 00:01:46,507
then the source path.

41
00:01:46,507 --> 00:01:49,329
Dash D says where to put the class files.

42
00:01:49,879 --> 00:01:53,548
Package com dot cloud cart dot pricing does not exist.

43
00:01:53,548 --> 00:01:56,946
Java C looked in its class path and found nothing.

44
00:01:56,946 --> 00:02:00,140
The second error is only a result of the first.

45
00:02:00,690 --> 00:02:03,824
Now tell java C where the dependency is.

46
00:02:03,824 --> 00:02:04,842
Type: java C,

47
00:02:04,842 --> 00:02:05,547
dash C P,

48
00:02:05,547 --> 00:02:07,584
lib slash pricing dot jar,

49
00:02:07,584 --> 00:02:08,132
dash D,

50
00:02:08,132 --> 00:02:08,446
out,

51
00:02:08,446 --> 00:02:10,013
and the source path.

52
00:02:10,563 --> 00:02:14,168
Silence. It compiled, because the jar was on the class path.

53
00:02:14,718 --> 00:02:18,707
Look at the output folder. Type: find, out, dash type, f.

54
00:02:19,257 --> 00:02:22,381
The class file sits in folders that match the package.

55
00:02:22,381 --> 00:02:24,463
Java builds the folder path for you.

56
00:02:25,013 --> 00:02:29,919
What is inside the jar? Type: jar, T F, lib slash pricing dot jar.

57
00:02:30,469 --> 00:02:33,020
A jar is just an archive of class files,

58
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:34,742
with the same folder paths.

59
00:02:34,742 --> 00:02:36,400
The tax class is in there.

60
00:02:36,950 --> 00:02:37,503
Run it.

61
00:02:37,503 --> 00:02:40,898
The class path now needs the output folder,

62
00:02:40,898 --> 00:02:41,845
and the jar,

63
00:02:41,845 --> 00:02:43,267
joined by a colon.

64
00:02:43,267 --> 00:02:44,135
Type: java,

65
00:02:44,135 --> 00:02:44,846
dash C P,

66
00:02:44,846 --> 00:02:47,688
out colon lib slash pricing dot jar,

67
00:02:47,688 --> 00:02:49,899
com dot cloud cart dot main.

68
00:02:50,449 --> 00:02:50,805
Total,

69
00:02:50,805 --> 00:02:51,873
one hundred eight.

70
00:02:51,873 --> 00:02:53,771
The tax class came from the jar.

71
00:02:53,771 --> 00:02:55,372
Notice the full class name,

72
00:02:55,372 --> 00:02:56,380
with its package.

73
00:02:58,430 --> 00:03:00,947
Go to the shop. Type: CD, shop.

74
00:03:01,497 --> 00:03:02,785
Compile it again,

75
00:03:02,785 --> 00:03:04,301
with the dependency.

76
00:03:04,301 --> 00:03:05,286
Type: java C,

77
00:03:05,286 --> 00:03:05,968
dash C P,

78
00:03:05,968 --> 00:03:07,938
lib slash pricing dot jar,

79
00:03:07,938 --> 00:03:08,468
dash D,

80
00:03:08,468 --> 00:03:08,771
out,

81
00:03:08,771 --> 00:03:10,287
and the source path.

82
00:03:10,837 --> 00:03:14,132
Now the classic mistake: run without the jar.

83
00:03:14,132 --> 00:03:14,938
Type: java,

84
00:03:14,938 --> 00:03:15,597
dash C P,

85
00:03:15,597 --> 00:03:15,889
out,

86
00:03:15,889 --> 00:03:16,988
the class name,

87
00:03:16,988 --> 00:03:19,551
then redirect errors to the screen,

88
00:03:19,551 --> 00:03:19,917
pipe,

89
00:03:19,917 --> 00:03:20,283
head,

90
00:03:20,283 --> 00:03:20,796
dash N,

91
00:03:20,796 --> 00:03:21,162
five.

92
00:03:21,712 --> 00:03:24,144
Look: store and currency print first.

93
00:03:24,144 --> 00:03:26,969
The program only needs the tax class later,

94
00:03:26,969 --> 00:03:28,086
so it fails late,

95
00:03:28,086 --> 00:03:30,058
with no class def found error.

96
00:03:30,058 --> 00:03:33,147
A missing jar on the server shows up like this.

97
00:03:33,697 --> 00:03:39,435
Another mistake: no class path at all. Type: java, com dot cloud cart dot main.

98
00:03:39,985 --> 00:03:42,102
Could not find or load main class.

99
00:03:42,102 --> 00:03:44,219
Java looked in the current folder,

100
00:03:44,219 --> 00:03:46,087
and found no com folder there.

101
00:03:46,637 --> 00:03:47,849
Now configuration.

102
00:03:47,849 --> 00:03:51,013
The program reads a variable called store name.

103
00:03:51,013 --> 00:03:52,966
Type: store name equals Bean,

104
00:03:52,966 --> 00:03:56,130
then the java command with the full class path.

105
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:57,458
Store: Bean.

106
00:03:57,458 --> 00:04:00,438
We changed behavior without touching the code.

107
00:04:00,438 --> 00:04:01,993
An environment variable,

108
00:04:01,993 --> 00:04:03,613
set for this one command.

109
00:04:04,163 --> 00:04:05,231
And a property.

110
00:04:05,231 --> 00:04:06,014
Type: java,

111
00:04:06,014 --> 00:04:08,079
dash D currency equals E U R,

112
00:04:08,079 --> 00:04:10,499
then the class path and the class.

113
00:04:11,049 --> 00:04:12,115
Currency: E U R.

114
00:04:12,115 --> 00:04:12,714
Same jar,

115
00:04:12,714 --> 00:04:13,846
same class files,

116
00:04:13,846 --> 00:04:15,111
different settings.

117
00:04:15,111 --> 00:04:16,044
In production,

118
00:04:16,044 --> 00:04:18,175
these come from the environment.

119
00:04:20,225 --> 00:04:21,974
Three messages, three fixes.

120
00:04:22,524 --> 00:04:28,092
Package does not exist, at compile time. Add the jar to java C with dash C P.

121
00:04:28,642 --> 00:04:33,549
No class def found error, at run time. Add the jar to the java class path.

122
00:04:34,099 --> 00:04:36,211
Could not find or load main class.

123
00:04:36,211 --> 00:04:37,702
Use the full class name,

124
00:04:37,702 --> 00:04:40,435
and put the output folder in the class path.

125
00:04:40,985 --> 00:04:43,521
And remember: configuration is not a bug.

126
00:04:43,521 --> 00:04:47,108
Check the variables and properties before you change code.

127
00:04:49,158 --> 00:04:50,067
Your lab task.

128
00:04:50,067 --> 00:04:53,507
Lab seventy-eight builds a small project and its jar.

129
00:04:53,507 --> 00:04:55,259
Lab check judges your work.

130
00:04:55,809 --> 00:04:57,927
It lives at git hub dot com,

131
00:04:57,927 --> 00:04:59,439
slash it dash waves,

132
00:04:59,439 --> 00:05:01,178
slash dev ops dash A I,

133
00:05:01,178 --> 00:05:02,010
in academy,

134
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:02,313
lab,

135
00:05:02,313 --> 00:05:04,279
lab seventy-eight dot S H.

136
00:05:04,829 --> 00:05:09,053
One: compile Main with the jar on the class path, into the out folder.

137
00:05:09,603 --> 00:05:14,189
Two: run it with the full class path. Save the output into run dot text.

138
00:05:14,739 --> 00:05:17,184
Three: run it with store name Bean,

139
00:05:17,184 --> 00:05:18,512
and currency E U R.

140
00:05:18,512 --> 00:05:21,097
Save the output into config dot text.

141
00:05:21,647 --> 00:05:26,255
Four: run it with the jar missing, and save the error into fail dot text.

142
00:05:26,805 --> 00:05:28,529
Five: answers dot text,

143
00:05:28,529 --> 00:05:29,429
three lines.

144
00:05:29,429 --> 00:05:31,003
Package: folder path.

145
00:05:31,003 --> 00:05:33,178
Class path: where java looks.

146
00:05:33,178 --> 00:05:34,527
Dependency: a jar.

147
00:05:35,077 --> 00:05:35,610
Install,

148
00:05:35,610 --> 00:05:36,409
then lab up,

149
00:05:36,409 --> 00:05:37,074
lab check,

150
00:05:37,074 --> 00:05:37,939
and lab down,

151
00:05:37,939 --> 00:05:38,738
like before.

152
00:05:38,738 --> 00:05:41,733
The shortcut file is shortcuts seventy-eight.

153
00:05:43,783 --> 00:05:45,852
Pass or fail. You need all six.

154
00:05:46,402 --> 00:05:48,216
Five pass lines in lab check.

155
00:05:48,766 --> 00:05:51,134
You can say how a package maps to folders.

156
00:05:51,684 --> 00:05:54,201
You can build a class path with a folder and a jar.

157
00:05:54,751 --> 00:05:58,548
You can say when the jar is needed: compile time and run time.

158
00:05:59,098 --> 00:06:02,874
You can change behavior with an environment variable and a property.

159
00:06:03,424 --> 00:06:05,344
lab down, nothing left behind.

160
00:06:05,894 --> 00:06:07,196
To pass, all six.

161
00:06:09,246 --> 00:06:12,083
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

162
00:06:12,633 --> 00:06:14,724
One: lab up, and read the task file.

163
00:06:15,274 --> 00:06:16,981
Two: compile with the jar.

164
00:06:17,531 --> 00:06:20,027
Three: run, and run with configuration.

165
00:06:20,577 --> 00:06:23,137
Four: break the class path, and keep the error.

166
00:06:23,687 --> 00:06:25,969
Five: write your answers, and lab check.

167
00:06:26,519 --> 00:06:29,101
Six: lab down, and prove nothing is left.

168
00:06:29,651 --> 00:06:31,485
Pause the video, and begin now.

169
00:06:47,035 --> 00:06:47,910
Quick check.

170
00:06:48,460 --> 00:06:50,422
How does a package name map to the disk?

171
00:06:50,972 --> 00:06:52,402
What goes in the class path?

172
00:06:52,952 --> 00:06:56,834
When do you need a dependency: compile time, run time, or both?

173
00:06:57,384 --> 00:06:59,816
Two ways to configure a program from outside?

174
00:07:00,366 --> 00:07:04,057
Objective covered: M C zero nine, objective three.

175
